  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Demand in core medical imaging is stable but growth is tepid, while the industrial segment remains a smaller contributor with limited momentum. Persistent cost headwinds are compressing margins, and the revenue trajectory suggests a slow, unspectacular recovery rather than a reacceleration. The full-year outlook points to a steady but uninspiring environment with no visible near-term catalyst.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership delivered gross margin at the high end of its own targets, signaling some operational discipline despite year-on-year erosion. Guidance ranges for the next quarter are wide but center roughly on consensus, suggesting a cautious rather than bold posture. A narrow earnings miss and minor insider selling add a subdued tone, and the narrative lacks a transformative initiative, leaving the market to view execution as competent but not yet compelling.",
